WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.881
Pocket Mockster is a complete monster-catching role-playing

00:00:02.881 --> 00:00:04.939
game, built entirely from scratch.

00:00:04.939 --> 00:00:07.820
It is written in TypeScript and rendered

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.878
on a plain HTML canvas.

00:00:09.878 --> 00:00:12.759
The whole thing runs in the browser,

00:00:12.759 --> 00:00:15.640
with no backend and no runtime dependencies.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.698
And here is the twist.

00:00:17.698 --> 00:00:20.579
An AI agent can play the entire

00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:22.225
game, to test it.

00:00:23.225 --> 00:00:26.278
At its heart, this is a classic

00:00:26.278 --> 00:00:27.151
creature-collecting adventure.

00:00:27.151 --> 00:00:30.204
You choose a starter, explore an overworld,

00:00:30.204 --> 00:00:33.257
and battle wild creatures and rival trainers.

00:00:33.257 --> 00:00:36.311
You catch new companions, train a team,

00:00:36.311 --> 00:00:38.055
and slowly grow stronger.

00:00:38.055 --> 00:00:41.109
The journey runs across eight gyms, all

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:44.162
the way to a final Champion fight.

00:00:45.162 --> 00:00:47.682
The story gives that journey a reason.

00:00:47.682 --> 00:00:50.202
The Mocca region runs on the Ledger,

00:00:50.202 --> 00:00:52.722
a stone record of every creature ever

00:00:52.722 --> 00:00:53.082
catalogued.

00:00:53.082 --> 00:00:55.603
A group called Team Rollback wants to

00:00:55.603 --> 00:00:58.123
revert the region to its first draft.

00:00:58.123 --> 00:01:00.643
And the very first entry in the

00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:03.163
Ledger, Originon, begins to stir at Null

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:03.523
Peak.

00:01:04.523 --> 00:01:07.282
Under the hood, the codebase is organized

00:01:07.282 --> 00:01:08.858
into four clear layers.

00:01:08.858 --> 00:01:11.617
An entry layer boots and runs the

00:01:11.617 --> 00:01:12.011
loop.

00:01:12.011 --> 00:01:14.769
A runtime layer holds all of the

00:01:14.769 --> 00:01:15.952
live game state.

00:01:15.952 --> 00:01:18.710
A content layer describes the world purely

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:19.499
as data.

00:01:19.499 --> 00:01:22.257
And a data layer defines every species,

00:01:22.257 --> 00:01:23.439
move, and item.

00:01:23.439 --> 00:01:26.198
Crucially, that data never changes at runtime.

00:01:26.198 --> 00:01:28.957
A live creature is built from a

00:01:28.957 --> 00:01:30.139
template on demand.

00:01:31.138 --> 00:01:33.735
Let's start at the entry point.

00:01:33.735 --> 00:01:36.765
The file main.ts runs a fixed sixty-hertz

00:01:36.765 --> 00:01:37.631
game loop.

00:01:37.631 --> 00:01:40.661
It advances the simulation in fixed time

00:01:40.661 --> 00:01:43.258
slices, then draws once per frame.

00:01:43.258 --> 00:01:46.288
A speed multiplier lets the tests and

00:01:46.288 --> 00:01:49.318
the agent fast-forward everything, which keeps every

00:01:49.318 --> 00:01:50.184
run deterministic.

00:01:50.184 --> 00:01:53.214
Because the logic is decoupled from rendering,

00:01:53.214 --> 00:01:56.244
the very same code can run headless

00:01:56.244 --> 00:01:57.110
in tests.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.247
At the center of the runtime sits

00:02:01.247 --> 00:02:02.592
the Game class.

00:02:02.592 --> 00:02:05.729
It works as a mode-driven state machine,

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:08.867
switching between the title, overworld, menus, and

00:02:08.867 --> 00:02:09.315
battle.

00:02:09.315 --> 00:02:12.452
Just as important, it implements a script

00:02:12.452 --> 00:02:13.349
host interface.

00:02:13.349 --> 00:02:16.486
That lets cutscenes and dialogue drive the

00:02:16.486 --> 00:02:19.175
game directly, without touching engine code.

00:02:20.175 --> 00:02:23.603
Combat lives in its own dedicated engine.

00:02:23.603 --> 00:02:27.030
It implements a canon-style damage formula, a

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:30.458
ten-type effectiveness chart, and the physical-special split.

00:02:30.458 --> 00:02:33.885
It also handles status conditions, weather, terrain,

00:02:33.885 --> 00:02:37.313
entry hazards, and a tiered trainer AI.

00:02:37.313 --> 00:02:40.740
Remarkably, all of that fits in about

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.209
one thousand lines.

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:45.636
The engine returns plain text messages, so

00:02:45.636 --> 00:02:49.064
it stays fully testable outside the browser.

00:02:50.065 --> 00:02:53.342
The world itself is data, not code.

00:02:53.342 --> 00:02:56.619
The content layer defines fifty-six maps, ninety-three

00:02:56.619 --> 00:02:58.492
trainers, and eight gyms.

00:02:58.492 --> 00:03:01.769
It also holds the encounter tables, items,

00:03:01.769 --> 00:03:03.173
and quest rewards.

00:03:03.173 --> 00:03:06.450
Before the game ships, a validator checks

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.259
that every single reference actually resolves.

00:03:09.259 --> 00:03:12.536
Adding a town or a gym means

00:03:12.536 --> 00:03:15.345
writing data, not rewiring the engine.

00:03:16.345 --> 00:03:19.447
Story beats run on a small scripting

00:03:19.447 --> 00:03:19.891
language.

00:03:19.891 --> 00:03:22.993
Script commands can speak lines, start battles,

00:03:22.993 --> 00:03:25.209
give items, and advance quests.

00:03:25.209 --> 00:03:28.311
A quest log tracks a thirteen-stage main

00:03:28.311 --> 00:03:31.414
journey, plus about a dozen side quests.

00:03:31.414 --> 00:03:34.516
Each one carries its own objective and

00:03:34.516 --> 00:03:36.289
its own journal entries.

00:03:37.289 --> 00:03:40.088
Presentation gets its own toolkit too.

00:03:40.088 --> 00:03:43.353
A frame-based sequence engine drives tweens, fades,

00:03:43.353 --> 00:03:44.753
and typewriter text.

00:03:44.753 --> 00:03:48.018
It powers a five-scene intro movie and

00:03:48.018 --> 00:03:49.884
the scrolling end credits.

00:03:49.884 --> 00:03:53.150
Your progress saves into any of three

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:56.415
slots, with backward compatibility for older saves.

00:03:57.415 --> 00:03:59.794
Now for the most unusual part.

00:03:59.794 --> 00:04:02.570
A Codex agent can play the live

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:04.553
game inside a real browser.

00:04:04.553 --> 00:04:07.329
It connects through a Model Context Protocol

00:04:07.329 --> 00:04:09.708
bridge to a small game server.

00:04:09.708 --> 00:04:12.484
Three personalities put it through its paces.

00:04:12.484 --> 00:04:15.260
A curious kid, a focused speedrunner, and

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:18.035
an adversarial tester trying to break things.

00:04:18.035 --> 00:04:20.811
Each run produces detailed logs and a

00:04:20.811 --> 00:04:23.587
written report of what the agent found.

00:04:24.586 --> 00:04:27.761
By the numbers, the project is compact

00:04:27.761 --> 00:04:28.668
but dense.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:31.844
It holds roughly nineteen thousand lines across

00:04:31.844 --> 00:04:34.112
a hundred and eleven files.

00:04:34.112 --> 00:04:37.287
That includes forty-one species, sixty-six moves, and

00:04:37.287 --> 00:04:38.194
ninety-three trainers.

00:04:38.194 --> 00:04:41.369
The Game class alone runs past two

00:04:41.369 --> 00:04:43.637
and a half thousand lines.

00:04:44.637 --> 00:04:47.841
Quality rests on several gates working together.

00:04:47.841 --> 00:04:51.045
Vitest covers the engine with a large

00:04:51.045 --> 00:04:51.960
unit suite.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.164
Playwright drives complete end-to-end journeys through the

00:04:55.164 --> 00:04:56.079
real browser.

00:04:56.079 --> 00:04:59.283
And the content validator catches broken maps,

00:04:59.283 --> 00:05:02.487
quests, and scripts early, long before they

00:05:02.487 --> 00:05:03.860
reach a player.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:07.064
Together, these gates let a solo developer

00:05:07.064 --> 00:05:08.895
refactor with real confidence.

00:05:09.894 --> 00:05:12.398
So here is the whole picture, in

00:05:12.398 --> 00:05:13.471
a single idea.

00:05:13.471 --> 00:05:15.976
An engine, a content layer, and a

00:05:15.976 --> 00:05:18.480
data layer, wrapped by a browser loop.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.984
It is a data-driven game, deep enough

00:05:20.984 --> 00:05:23.488
that an agent can play it on

00:05:23.488 --> 00:05:24.204
its own.

00:05:24.204 --> 00:05:25.635
That is Pocket Mockster.
